{"ts": "2026-09-21T02:35:00Z", "event": "task_done", "plan": "260920-qcrrqs-macos-support", "phase": 4, "task": "TASK-025..031", "message": "just dist's native-vs-cross heuristic now compares vendor+OS (not full triple, not just arch) -- deliberately not comparing the full triple, since that would have broken the existing gnu-host/musl-target case this repo already relies on. Archive step detects gtar, falls back to GNU-tar-as-tar, falls back to plain BSD-compatible tar with a stderr note about lost reproducibility. Checksum step forks sha256sum/shasum -a 256. release.yml matrix expanded to {target,runner} pairs (musl/ubuntu-latest, both darwin triples/macos-latest); musl-toolchain step conditioned on the linux row; confirmed the dist/attest/upload steps already interpolate matrix.target with no hard-coded asset name. README documents the three-asset release and PINST_BUILD_FROM_SOURCE.", "detail": {}}
